  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Infinite Series [S+N]\n\nAn infinite series $\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty a_n$ is shorthand for the limit of partial sums $s_N = \\sum_{n=1}^N a_n$. The series **converges** if $(s_N)$ converges as a sequence; otherwise it diverges. So everything from notebook 1 about sequences applies — but with a twist: now the question is about the *cumulative* effect.\n\nThree classical workhorses:\n\n- **Geometric series** $\\sum r^n$ converges iff $|r| < 1$, with sum $1/(1-r)$.\n- **p-series** $\\sum 1/n^p$ converges iff $p > 1$.\n- **Alternating series** $\\sum (-1)^{n+1} b_n$ with $b_n \\downarrow 0$ converges (Leibniz).\n\nThis notebook exercises convergence tests, distinguishes absolute from conditional convergence, and ends with the Riemann rearrangement theorem — proof that \"sum\" is more subtle than \"add the terms\".\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Geometric series\n\n$\\sum r^n = 1/(1-r)$ for $|r| < 1$. Watch the partial sums march toward the closed-form limit.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "r_val : 0.7$\nN : 50$\ns_partial : []$\nrunning : 0.0$\nfor n : 0 thru N do (\n  running : running + r_val^n,\n  s_partial : endcons(running, s_partial))$\nlimit_val : 1.0 / (1 - r_val)$\nprint(\"closed-form sum: 1/(1-0.7) =\", limit_val)$\nprint(\"s_50 =\", last(s_partial))$\nprint(\"error:\", abs(limit_val - last(s_partial)))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", marker_size=4, name=\"partial sum s_N\",\n  points(makelist(n, n, 0, N), s_partial),\n  color=\"red\", dash=\"dash\", name=\"1/(1-r)\",\n  explicit(limit_val, t, 0, N),\n  title=\"Geometric series r=0.7 — partial sums converge to 1/(1-r)\",\n  xlabel=\"N\", ylabel=\"s_N\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 16,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "closed-form sum: 1/(1-0.7) = 3.333333333333333\ns_50 = 3.333333291369147\nerror: 4.1964185903964335e-8"
          ]
        },
