    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## p-series and the integral test [S+N]\n\n$\\sum 1/n^p$ converges iff $p > 1$. The **integral test** says $\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty f(n)$ and $\\int_1^\\infty f$ have the same convergence status when $f$ is positive, decreasing. Maxima can compute the integral and confirm.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "assume(p > 1)$\nprint(\"∫₁^∞ 1/x^p dx for p > 1:\")$\nintegrate(1/x^p, x, 1, inf);\nforget(p > 1)$\nprint(\"(equals 1/(p-1) for p > 1; diverges for p ≤ 1)\")$\nprint()$\nprint(\"p = 2: harmonic-squared sum is the Basel problem, value π²/6 ≈\", float(%pi^2/6))$\nprint(\"p = 1: harmonic series diverges (logarithmic)\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "∫₁^∞ 1/x^p dx for p > 1:\n1/(p-1)\n(equals 1/(p-1) for p > 1; diverges for p ≤ 1)\np = 2: harmonic-squared sum is the Basel problem, value π²/6 ≈\n  1.6449340668482262\np = 1: harmonic series diverges (logarithmic)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Visualise: p = 0.5 (diverges), p = 1.0 (the harmonic series — diverges, slowly), p = 2.0 (converges).\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "p_vals : [0.5, 1.0, 2.0]$\nN_show : 100$\nn_grid : makelist(n, n, 1, N_show)$\nsums_by_p : []$\nfor p in p_vals do block([s, run, n],\n  s : [], run : 0.0,\n  for n : 1 thru N_show do (\n    run : run + 1.0 / float(n^p),\n    s : endcons(run, s)),\n  sums_by_p : endcons(s, sums_by_p))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"red\", line_width=2, name=\"p = 0.5 (diverges, fast)\",\n  lines(n_grid, sums_by_p[1]),\n  color=\"orange\", line_width=2, name=\"p = 1.0 (harmonic, log-divergent)\",\n  lines(n_grid, sums_by_p[2]),\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=2, name=\"p = 2.0 (Basel, converges to π²/6)\",\n  lines(n_grid, sums_by_p[3]),\n  color=\"black\", dash=\"dash\", name=\"π²/6\",\n  explicit(float(%pi^2/6), t, 1, N_show),\n  title=\"p-series partial sums\",\n  xlabel=\"N\", ylabel=\"Σ 1/n^p\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
