    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Ratio and root tests\n\nFor $\\sum a_n$ with positive terms, define $L = \\lim_{n\\to\\infty} a_{n+1}/a_n$ (ratio test) or $L = \\limsup_{n\\to\\infty} |a_n|^{1/n}$ (root test). Then:\n\n- $L < 1$ ⇒ convergent\n- $L > 1$ ⇒ divergent\n- $L = 1$ ⇒ inconclusive (harmonic and Basel both have $L = 1$)\n\nExample: $\\sum n^2 / 2^n$. Ratio: $\\lim (n+1)^2 / n^2 \\cdot 1/2 = 1/2 < 1$ — converges.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "a_n_func(n) := n^2 / 2^n$\nratios : map(lambda([n], float(a_n_func(n+1) / a_n_func(n))), [1, 5, 10, 20, 50])$\nprint(\"ratios a_{n+1}/a_n at n =\", [1, 5, 10, 20, 50], \":\", ratios)$\nprint(\"→ 1/2 in the limit, confirming convergence\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 19,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "ratios a_{n+1}/a_n at n = [1,5,10,20,50] : [2.0,0.72,0.605,0.55125,0.5202]\n→ 1/2 in the limit, confirming convergence"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Absolute vs conditional convergence\n\n$\\sum a_n$ is **absolutely convergent** if $\\sum |a_n|$ converges, **conditionally convergent** if $\\sum a_n$ converges but $\\sum |a_n|$ doesn't.\n\nThe classic conditional series: $\\sum (-1)^{n+1}/n = 1 - 1/2 + 1/3 - \\ldots = \\ln 2$. Yet $\\sum 1/n$ diverges.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "N_alt : 100$\nalt_partial : []$\nabs_partial : []$\nrun_alt : 0.0$ run_abs : 0.0$\nfor n : 1 thru N_alt do (\n  run_alt : run_alt + (-1.0)^(n+1) / float(n),\n  run_abs : run_abs + 1.0 / float(n),\n  alt_partial : endcons(run_alt, alt_partial),\n  abs_partial : endcons(run_abs, abs_partial))$\n\nprint(\"Σ_{n=1}^100 (-1)^(n+1)/n  =\", last(alt_partial))$\nprint(\"Σ_{n=1}^100 1/n           =\", last(abs_partial))$\nprint(\"ln(2) ≈\", float(log(2)))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=2, name=\"alternating Σ (-1)^(n+1)/n\",\n  lines(makelist(n, n, 1, N_alt), alt_partial),\n  color=\"red\", dash=\"dash\", name=\"ln(2)\",\n  explicit(float(log(2)), t, 1, N_alt),\n  title=\"Alternating harmonic — conditionally convergent to ln(2)\",\n  xlabel=\"N\", ylabel=\"partial sum\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 20,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Σ_{n=1}^100 (-1)^(n+1)/n  = 0.688172179310195\nΣ_{n=1}^100 1/n           = 5.187377517639621\nln(2) ≈ 0.6931471805599453"
          ]
        },
        {
